1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:04,045
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,511 --> 00:00:14,097
[Diego] <i>I still believe</i>
<i>there's hope for this town.</i>

3
00:00:14,180 --> 00:00:16,933
<i>No matter what you do,</i>
<i>you can't change their lives.</i>

4
00:00:17,017 --> 00:00:19,894
<i>Not as long as this family is in power.</i>

5
00:00:19,978 --> 00:00:26,234
[Ivy] <i>I feel nothing but pain,</i>
<i>anger, and fury.</i>

6
00:00:26,317 --> 00:00:30,321
<i>I promise you and Dad,</i>
<i>I'll avenge your deaths.</i>

7
00:00:30,405 --> 00:00:32,115
[screaming]

8
00:00:32,198 --> 00:00:34,075
[Diego] <i>Their project here</i>
<i>will push through.</i>

9
00:00:34,159 --> 00:00:38,288
<i>They got more funds from</i>
<i>the huge amount Ivy Aguas invested.</i>

10
00:00:38,371 --> 00:00:41,291
[woman] <i>The congressman's statue</i>
<i>was destroyed last night.</i>

11
00:00:41,374 --> 00:00:44,419
[Julio] <i>Monitor who goes</i>
<i>in and out of town.</i>

12
00:00:44,502 --> 00:00:47,297
<i>Do a background check on all of them.</i>

13
00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:51,384
-[Emilia] Does this include, Ivy?
-Especially Ivy.

14
00:00:51,468 --> 00:00:55,764
[Julio] <i>These things started</i>
<i>the moment she came here.</i>

15
00:00:55,847 --> 00:00:57,557
[Emilia] <i>I'll uncover her deepest secrets.</i>

16
00:00:57,640 --> 00:01:01,978
<i>Governor, now that someone's openly</i>
<i>going against you, it's troubling.</i>

17
00:01:02,062 --> 00:01:03,813
<i>I'm starting to reconsider my investment.</i>

18
00:01:03,897 --> 00:01:05,356
[Julio] <i>We have to fix this.</i>

19
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:09,152
<i>We need that woman and her money.</i>

20
00:01:09,235 --> 00:01:13,031
<i>Talk to Arnaldo.</i>
<i>He can handle this better than you.</i>

21
00:01:13,114 --> 00:01:13,948
[Arthur]<i> I saw them.</i>

22
00:01:14,032 --> 00:01:17,952
<i>A woman and a man had a sledgehammer.</i>

23
00:01:18,036 --> 00:01:19,829
<i>They destroyed the statue.</i>

24
00:01:19,913 --> 00:01:22,624
<i>This is the first and last time</i>

25
00:01:22,707 --> 00:01:26,044
<i>that I let anyone openly oppose me.</i>

26
00:01:26,127 --> 00:01:28,713
[ominous music playing]

27
00:01:32,050 --> 00:01:33,176
Ma.

28
00:01:34,052 --> 00:01:35,720
Stop worrying.

29
00:01:35,804 --> 00:01:39,724
Grandpa is right. I know
how to charm Ivy. We won't lose her.

30
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:42,644
And who will handle the investigation?

31
00:01:42,727 --> 00:01:44,854
Shouldn't we prioritize that?

32
00:01:45,480 --> 00:01:48,233
And while you're at it, maybe, you know,

33
00:01:48,316 --> 00:01:52,904
I should take her to the best spa
to relax, take her shopping…

34
00:01:52,987 --> 00:01:55,240
Stop. Stop.

35
00:01:55,323 --> 00:01:57,117
You'll just embarrass yourself.

36
00:01:57,742 --> 00:02:00,912
She's a strong woman.
She won't get swayed by petty things.

37
00:02:00,995 --> 00:02:03,414
She will respond better
to a strong man like me.

38
00:02:03,498 --> 00:02:06,876
Hey, are you trying to say
that I'm weak? Is that it?

39
00:02:06,960 --> 00:02:08,962
Mom, that's not what I meant.

40
00:02:09,045 --> 00:02:10,922
You're the strongest woman I know.

41
00:02:12,090 --> 00:02:14,425
It's just that…
Ivy's pretty much fallen for me.

42
00:02:15,468 --> 00:02:17,804
It'd be easier for us
if you let me do this.

43
00:02:19,180 --> 00:02:21,558
Fine. Do whatever you think is needed.

44
00:02:21,641 --> 00:02:24,769
But you cannot fail. 'Cause if you do so,

45
00:02:24,853 --> 00:02:27,981
then your grandpa will put
all the blame on me! Do you understand?

46
00:02:29,649 --> 00:02:32,735
I understand. Don't worry.

47
00:02:34,571 --> 00:02:37,323
Oh, while I'm out with Ivy,
can you please handle Natalie for me?

48
00:02:38,658 --> 00:02:39,576
Fine.

49
00:02:39,659 --> 00:02:42,662
[tense music playing]

50
00:02:43,371 --> 00:02:44,372
Madrigal…

51
00:02:45,331 --> 00:02:46,791
take the night off. I have a date.

52
00:02:48,459 --> 00:02:50,044
-Thank you, Mayor.
-Sure.

53
00:02:53,089 --> 00:02:54,549
[Pandoy] Mr. Fernan, we'll take care…
of the delivery.

54
00:02:54,632 --> 00:02:55,675
All right. Are you sure?

55
00:02:55,758 --> 00:02:57,176
-Yeah.
-Make sure you weigh them right.

56
00:02:57,260 --> 00:02:59,262
I know, don't worry.

57
00:02:59,345 --> 00:03:00,305
We already talked.

58
00:03:00,388 --> 00:03:03,391
-Take this with you.
-Wow! That was sweet!

59
00:03:03,474 --> 00:03:06,352
-Take care, okay?
-You're so sweet!

60
00:03:06,436 --> 00:03:08,938
-A kiss for good luck?
-[laughing]

61
00:03:09,022 --> 00:03:11,900
-Oh, you. Stop being so silly.
-Come on, Auntie. Just a peck.

62
00:03:11,983 --> 00:03:13,359
Wait. That's it?

63
00:03:13,443 --> 00:03:15,153
[laughing]

64
00:03:15,236 --> 00:03:16,654
-Just stick close behind us, okay?
-All right.

65
00:03:16,738 --> 00:03:18,281
-I'll load these on the truck.
-Stay safe, okay?

66
00:03:18,364 --> 00:03:20,325
-We will.
-[Loring] All right then.

67
00:03:20,992 --> 00:03:22,577
[Pandoy] No drinking, okay?

68
00:03:22,660 --> 00:03:23,786
[man] All right.

69
00:03:25,121 --> 00:03:27,290
-Have a safe trip.
-Take care.

70
00:03:29,500 --> 00:03:30,460
-Nanny. Well…
-Yes?

71
00:03:30,543 --> 00:03:32,378
-I have to go now too.
-Take this with you.

72
00:03:32,462 --> 00:03:34,088
-Oh. I'll just put it here.
-Okay then.

73
00:03:34,172 --> 00:03:36,257
Take care, all right?

74
00:03:36,341 --> 00:03:38,718
-Thank you.
-You never know nowadays.

75
00:03:38,801 --> 00:03:40,637
All right. I'll be going now.

76
00:03:40,720 --> 00:03:43,097
Oh, by the way, how is your grandpa?

77
00:03:43,181 --> 00:03:44,891
Do they have a suspect yet?

78
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:46,643
Not yet.

79
00:03:46,726 --> 00:03:49,354
It might just be a prank.

80
00:03:49,437 --> 00:03:51,314
-Go now.
-All right, Nanny.

81
00:03:51,397 --> 00:03:52,732
Don't let them leave you behind.

82
00:03:52,815 --> 00:03:54,692
-Take care.
-I will.

83
00:03:57,779 --> 00:03:59,948
-Have some coffee.
-Thank you.

84
00:04:00,031 --> 00:04:01,199
-Jepoy.
-Yes?

85
00:04:01,783 --> 00:04:04,869
You have to keep an eye on Emilia
while I distract Arnaldo.

86
00:04:06,204 --> 00:04:08,122
I have to know what she might be up to.

87
00:04:08,206 --> 00:04:09,332
Got it.

88
00:04:10,250 --> 00:04:13,169
I'm also keeping an eye
on a crazy man at the plaza.

89
00:04:13,253 --> 00:04:14,254
I think he knows something.

90
00:04:14,796 --> 00:04:15,630
You handle that.

91
00:04:15,713 --> 00:04:17,257
[doorbell ringing]

92
00:04:17,924 --> 00:04:18,800
My date is here.

93
00:04:18,883 --> 00:04:20,134
Ivy.

94
00:04:20,218 --> 00:04:22,595
[somber music playing]

95
00:04:22,679 --> 00:04:24,681
Be careful around that man, okay?

96
00:04:26,516 --> 00:04:27,600
I will.

97
00:04:36,901 --> 00:04:38,278
Does Natalie know about this?

98
00:04:39,445 --> 00:04:41,364
I don't want her feeling jealous.

99
00:04:41,447 --> 00:04:43,241
She has nothing to be jealous of.

100
00:04:44,826 --> 00:04:45,994
We aren't doing anything wrong.

101
00:04:47,453 --> 00:04:49,205
Well, it depends on…

102
00:04:49,289 --> 00:04:52,166
what's written
on the contract you brought.

103
00:04:53,501 --> 00:04:55,003
So, tell me, Mr. Mayor.

104
00:04:55,086 --> 00:04:58,589
Why did you have to take
me out on a romantic evening?

105
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:02,176
Uh… Well, to convince you.

106
00:05:04,262 --> 00:05:06,723
So you won't pull
your investment on my project.

107
00:05:07,265 --> 00:05:10,310
Oh, so the governor already told you.

108
00:05:10,393 --> 00:05:12,437
We don't keep secrets from each other.

109
00:05:13,187 --> 00:05:15,773
I don't like secrets either.

110
00:05:16,357 --> 00:05:18,359
We think alike, Mr. Mayor.

111
00:05:18,443 --> 00:05:20,862
So you should tell me now

112
00:05:20,945 --> 00:05:23,406
if you're hiding something
about the project.

113
00:05:25,950 --> 00:05:27,285
[Arnaldo] Well…

114
00:05:27,368 --> 00:05:31,581
Just a minor glitch.
The land we're planning to use

115
00:05:31,664 --> 00:05:33,875
is currently occupied by farmers.

116
00:05:34,751 --> 00:05:36,627
But don't worry. We'll force them out.

117
00:05:36,711 --> 00:05:38,004
What?

118
00:05:38,963 --> 00:05:42,216
Mr. Mayor, you assured me
there wouldn't be problems.

119
00:05:43,301 --> 00:05:45,636
I don't want to be involved in that.

120
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:47,722
We can't force them out.

121
00:05:47,805 --> 00:05:49,307
That's illegal dispersal!

122
00:05:49,974 --> 00:05:53,853
There are too many issues
for such a small project.

123
00:05:54,520 --> 00:05:57,774
I'd rather invest somewhere else.

124
00:05:58,649 --> 00:05:59,650
[chuckles]

125
00:06:00,818 --> 00:06:02,987
Ms. Aguas, don't drop me like this.

126
00:06:03,738 --> 00:06:05,740
This is why
I'm taking you out on a special date.

127
00:06:05,823 --> 00:06:06,866
To convince you.

128
00:06:09,911 --> 00:06:11,871
Come on, just give me a chance.

129
00:06:13,748 --> 00:06:16,084
I'm all for second chances, Mr. Mayor.

130
00:06:16,167 --> 00:06:19,879
Just make sure it's worthy of my time.

131
00:06:19,962 --> 00:06:23,841
[tense music playing]

132
00:06:35,603 --> 00:06:37,230
[Pandoy] Good evening, sir.
What's the problem?

133
00:06:37,313 --> 00:06:38,731
-[cop] Get down.
-[Pandoy] Sorry?

134
00:06:38,815 --> 00:06:40,358
-[Pandoy] What for?
-Get out!

135
00:06:42,068 --> 00:06:43,486
-What is it, officer?
-Get out of the car!

136
00:06:43,569 --> 00:06:45,196
-Get down.
-Sir… Sir. Sir.

137
00:06:45,279 --> 00:06:46,447
-That hurt.
-Sir!

138
00:06:46,531 --> 00:06:49,325
Be careful with those,
we still have to deliver them!

139
00:06:49,408 --> 00:06:50,535
Don't destroy them!

140
00:06:51,452 --> 00:06:53,412
Sir, we're going to deliver those!

141
00:06:53,496 --> 00:06:55,832
Let me go! I said let me go!

142
00:06:55,915 --> 00:06:57,625
[clamoring]

143
00:06:57,708 --> 00:06:58,543
Sir…

144
00:06:59,210 --> 00:07:00,461
[man grunting]

145
00:07:00,545 --> 00:07:02,880
[Diego] Hey! Hey, that's enough!

146
00:07:02,964 --> 00:07:05,675
Stop it! What do you think you're doing?

147
00:07:06,467 --> 00:07:10,304
Huh? What is this?
That's enough! I said that's enough!

148
00:07:12,014 --> 00:07:13,683
-What's happening?
-Ivy, stay here.

149
00:07:13,766 --> 00:07:14,725
I'll see what's going on.

150
00:07:14,809 --> 00:07:17,645
Diego Ardiente,
we're just following our orders.

151
00:07:17,728 --> 00:07:18,813
[action music playing]

152
00:07:18,896 --> 00:07:21,858
Was hurting people
part of your orders, huh?

153
00:07:22,692 --> 00:07:23,943
You jerk!

154
00:07:24,026 --> 00:07:26,279
Stop it! Stop!

155
00:07:26,362 --> 00:07:27,613
[men grunting]

156
00:07:27,697 --> 00:07:29,407
Stop!

157
00:07:29,490 --> 00:07:30,825
-[gunshot]
-[cop] So you won't stop?

158
00:07:35,913 --> 00:07:36,914
Stay here.

159
00:07:37,623 --> 00:07:39,292
Diego! What happened here?

160
00:07:39,375 --> 00:07:40,376
Ask them!

161
00:07:41,335 --> 00:07:43,254
Chief, what's going on?
Put your guns down.

162
00:07:43,838 --> 00:07:45,047
Put them down.

163
00:07:45,631 --> 00:07:47,091
All of you, over here.

164
00:07:47,175 --> 00:07:48,050
Our crops.

165
00:07:49,051 --> 00:07:51,012
-Let me…
-Our harvest!

166
00:07:51,971 --> 00:07:53,598
Let me do that, Mr. Pandoy.

167
00:07:53,681 --> 00:07:56,100
-Mr. Pandoy, let us do that.
-[Pandoy] I'm going to help.

168
00:07:56,184 --> 00:07:57,935
No. We've got this.

169
00:07:58,019 --> 00:08:01,063
[tense music playing]

170
00:08:02,315 --> 00:08:03,274
Stay away from us!

171
00:08:07,403 --> 00:08:08,863
We don't need your help.

172
00:08:15,661 --> 00:08:16,871
[Pandoy groans]

173
00:08:17,747 --> 00:08:18,998
They're ruined.

174
00:08:31,093 --> 00:08:32,720
You're taking the cops' side?

175
00:08:32,803 --> 00:08:34,514
Didn't you see
how they hurt those farmers?

176
00:08:34,597 --> 00:08:37,058
The farmers started it,
and you even joined in!

177
00:08:37,141 --> 00:08:38,768
They were destroying our crops!

178
00:08:38,851 --> 00:08:40,394
They were only doing their job!

179
00:08:40,478 --> 00:08:41,979
Was that part of their job?

180
00:08:42,688 --> 00:08:45,816
Just admit that they're abusing their
power because you're tolerating them!

181
00:08:45,900 --> 00:08:47,276
That's enough!

182
00:08:47,360 --> 00:08:49,654
You better show me some respect.

183
00:08:49,737 --> 00:08:51,239
I'm your brother.

184
00:08:51,322 --> 00:08:54,075
I'm older than you,
and above all, I'm the mayor!

185
00:08:54,158 --> 00:08:55,493
[Diego] That's the problem.

186
00:08:55,576 --> 00:08:56,494
You're the mayor.

187
00:08:57,286 --> 00:08:59,288
You're supposed to be
defending the helpless.

188
00:08:59,372 --> 00:09:01,666
But what are you doing?

189
00:09:01,749 --> 00:09:03,376
-[Emilia] Hey! Enough!
-You're taking advantage of them!

190
00:09:03,459 --> 00:09:05,753
-Me?
-Enough!

191
00:09:05,836 --> 00:09:09,632
Why are you two fighting again?
Stop this right now!

192
00:09:18,349 --> 00:09:22,270
[tense music playing]

193
00:09:28,401 --> 00:09:29,527
[loud thump]

194
00:09:36,576 --> 00:09:37,451
Ivy…

195
00:09:39,870 --> 00:09:42,331
I'm… I'm sorry.
I didn't want this to happen.

196
00:09:43,207 --> 00:09:44,875
Ivy, whatever happened…

197
00:09:45,876 --> 00:09:47,253
we are really sorry about it.

198
00:09:48,629 --> 00:09:49,630
It's okay.

199
00:09:51,382 --> 00:09:53,217
I think I better go home now.

200
00:09:53,301 --> 00:09:55,845
-Let me drive you home.
-No, no. It's fine.

201
00:09:55,928 --> 00:09:57,138
I asked my driver to pick me up.

202
00:09:58,472 --> 00:09:59,348
Governor.

203
00:10:04,562 --> 00:10:06,981
[Raul] Where did you hear
that news, Auntie?

204
00:10:08,274 --> 00:10:10,318
From someone I know at the market.

205
00:10:10,401 --> 00:10:13,946
She heard from her vegetable supplier
at Ardiente

206
00:10:14,030 --> 00:10:16,616
that the statue was destroyed.

207
00:10:16,699 --> 00:10:20,620
Hasn't your son or your wife
called you yet?

208
00:10:20,703 --> 00:10:22,538
The reception's bad here.

209
00:10:23,039 --> 00:10:26,334
I rarely get a decent signal, anyway.

210
00:10:26,417 --> 00:10:29,295
Actually, that's why I like it here.

211
00:10:29,378 --> 00:10:30,880
Life is more peaceful.

212
00:10:31,631 --> 00:10:33,341
I'm just worried…

213
00:10:33,424 --> 00:10:37,345
that your absence there
might get you into trouble.

214
00:10:39,138 --> 00:10:40,139
Don't worry about that.

215
00:10:41,724 --> 00:10:42,850
I'll take care of it.

216
00:10:44,060 --> 00:10:45,353
I'll go home tomorrow.

217
00:10:45,978 --> 00:10:48,105
I'll spend the night here.

218
00:10:48,814 --> 00:10:51,484
Auntie, give that to me. I'll feed her.

219
00:10:51,567 --> 00:10:53,694
-Okay.
-All right.

220
00:10:53,778 --> 00:10:57,740
[somber music playing]

221
00:11:08,793 --> 00:11:11,796
[action music playing]

222
00:11:26,602 --> 00:11:28,020
[thinking] <i>Stop it, Jepoy.</i>

223
00:11:28,104 --> 00:11:30,481
<i>You shouldn't want what you can't have.</i>

224
00:11:54,713 --> 00:11:56,882
-Hey. How are you?
-[man] We're okay, Mr. Diego.

225
00:11:56,966 --> 00:11:57,800
Where's Nanny?

226
00:11:57,883 --> 00:12:00,136
-She's right there.
-Nanny!

227
00:12:01,512 --> 00:12:02,847
[crying]

228
00:12:04,598 --> 00:12:07,226
Nanny, any update? How's Uncle?

229
00:12:08,310 --> 00:12:13,149
He broke some bones. He might need a cast.

230
00:12:14,483 --> 00:12:16,152
He's in the X-ray room.

231
00:12:17,111 --> 00:12:18,988
What'll happen now?

232
00:12:19,989 --> 00:12:22,867
Nanny, don't worry.

233
00:12:22,950 --> 00:12:25,202
I'll take care of Uncle Pandoy.

234
00:12:27,329 --> 00:12:28,581
I have some money saved.

235
00:12:31,584 --> 00:12:33,586
This is too much, Diego.

236
00:12:34,837 --> 00:12:35,963
Nanny,

237
00:12:36,839 --> 00:12:38,549
you don't have to be ashamed.

238
00:12:40,009 --> 00:12:42,178
You and Uncle Pandoy are basically family.

239
00:12:43,762 --> 00:12:46,015
Let me do this for you.

240
00:12:48,767 --> 00:12:52,062
[sobbing]

241
00:12:53,189 --> 00:12:54,648
Thank you.

242
00:12:55,524 --> 00:12:56,984
Anything for you.

243
00:13:00,029 --> 00:13:01,780
Ma'am, their bills have already been paid.

244
00:13:02,364 --> 00:13:05,534
-[Carlotta] What?
-Mr. Diego Ardiente-Torillo settled them.

245
00:13:05,618 --> 00:13:08,287
Is that so? All right, miss. Thank you.

246
00:13:10,456 --> 00:13:14,585
Sweetie, Diego has already paid the bills.

247
00:13:18,297 --> 00:13:21,967
Let's go before someone sees you here.

248
00:13:22,760 --> 00:13:26,764
["Sa'yo" by Silent Sanctuary playing]

249
00:13:58,963 --> 00:14:02,007
[action music playing]

250
00:14:20,693 --> 00:14:24,989
[tense music playing]

251
00:14:38,335 --> 00:14:39,587
[heavy breathing]

252
00:14:50,556 --> 00:14:54,059
[tense music playing]

253
00:15:19,043 --> 00:15:22,796
[thinking] <i>Dante? Ivy's father?</i>

254
00:15:30,679 --> 00:15:34,683
[eerie music playing]

255
00:15:45,444 --> 00:15:48,280
The Ardientes will soon fall.

256
00:15:50,240 --> 00:15:53,369
[evil laughing]

257
00:15:54,787 --> 00:15:58,874
A rival to match them.

258
00:16:00,042 --> 00:16:01,502
That woman.

259
00:16:03,545 --> 00:16:05,506
The woman who destroyed the statue!

260
00:16:06,507 --> 00:16:08,258
[Arthur laughing]

261
00:16:21,271 --> 00:16:22,773
-Mayor?
-Madrigal.

262
00:16:23,983 --> 00:16:26,652
It's so unlike you to come in this late.

263
00:16:27,403 --> 00:16:28,237
I'm sorry, Mayor.

264
00:16:28,320 --> 00:16:29,738
Where were you last night?

265
00:16:32,241 --> 00:16:33,909
-Uh…
-Never mind.

266
00:16:34,743 --> 00:16:37,329
What you do on your personal time
is none of my business.

267
00:16:37,413 --> 00:16:40,374
The policemen from last night
weren't from Ardiente, right?

268
00:16:41,583 --> 00:16:43,961
They don't know how things work here.

269
00:16:45,004 --> 00:16:49,049
There wouldn't have been
any trouble if they didn't start it.

270
00:16:51,301 --> 00:16:53,095
Make sure to sanction them.

271
00:16:53,178 --> 00:16:55,389
All of them, especially
the one who fired a gun.

272
00:16:57,057 --> 00:17:00,019
I don't want to hear
those farmers whine about me,

273
00:17:00,102 --> 00:17:01,478
or the Ardiente family.

274
00:17:02,229 --> 00:17:07,067
I'm sure their egos have grown
after what Diego did.

275
00:17:09,069 --> 00:17:11,071
I've really had it with Diego.

276
00:17:11,155 --> 00:17:13,407
[tense music playing]

277
00:17:16,994 --> 00:17:18,203
[Ivy] Nanny Carlotta?

278
00:17:18,287 --> 00:17:19,121
-Yes?
-Is everything ready?

279
00:17:19,204 --> 00:17:21,081
Yes, we'll load them into the car.

280
00:17:23,042 --> 00:17:24,460
Calm down, dear.

281
00:17:25,169 --> 00:17:28,130
The farmers are fine now.
They'll be discharged today.

282
00:17:28,881 --> 00:17:31,133
How can I calm down?

283
00:17:31,967 --> 00:17:34,678
They were hurt because of me.

284
00:17:34,762 --> 00:17:37,347
That's why we'll give them
a little something.

285
00:17:38,432 --> 00:17:40,309
What happened wasn't your fault.

286
00:17:40,392 --> 00:17:41,727
You didn't want that to happen.

287
00:17:41,810 --> 00:17:44,646
This was all the Ardientes' doing.

288
00:17:44,730 --> 00:17:47,441
Don't you dare blame yourself, Ivy.

289
00:17:47,524 --> 00:17:49,109
Let's go now. Come on.

290
00:17:49,193 --> 00:17:51,028
-All right.
-Before it gets too dark.

291
00:17:51,111 --> 00:17:53,072
-I'll help.
-No, it's okay. Let's go.

292
00:17:53,155 --> 00:17:55,407
-Please. Let me help.
-Bring everything to the car!

293
00:17:55,491 --> 00:17:56,533
Faster!

294
00:17:56,617 --> 00:17:57,910
-You don't have to--
-Let's move faster!

295
00:17:58,911 --> 00:18:00,913
-[Loring] Oh, Diego…
-[sighs]

296
00:18:01,497 --> 00:18:04,708
We can't thank you enough.

297
00:18:06,460 --> 00:18:10,964
Nanny, just feed me a lot of
banana fritters, and I'm good.

298
00:18:11,048 --> 00:18:13,509
-Okay, if that's what you want.
-[Pandoy chuckling]

299
00:18:13,592 --> 00:18:15,969
-Loring, Pandoy. Diego.
-Mr. Fernan.

300
00:18:16,053 --> 00:18:17,346
What's that?

301
00:18:17,429 --> 00:18:22,726
Uh… Here's a little gift
from the Ardientes.

302
00:18:22,810 --> 00:18:25,479
I told you they'd never let us down.

303
00:18:26,396 --> 00:18:29,149
Come on, Fernan. Stop fooling yourself.

304
00:18:29,233 --> 00:18:31,735
After what happened to our friends?

305
00:18:31,819 --> 00:18:33,362
After what they did to them?

306
00:18:33,445 --> 00:18:36,782
A little gift is enough to buy your vote?

307
00:18:36,865 --> 00:18:38,075
Whatever, Loring.

308
00:18:38,158 --> 00:18:40,369
It's up to you if you'll accept it or not.

309
00:18:40,452 --> 00:18:42,746
Mr. Fernan, who dropped by?

310
00:18:42,830 --> 00:18:44,373
Was it the mayor or the governor?

311
00:18:44,456 --> 00:18:47,918
No, it was actually
the pretty Ms. Ivy Aguas.

312
00:18:48,001 --> 00:18:50,254
I think she's the investor in the project.

313
00:18:50,337 --> 00:18:53,549
[tense music playing]

314
00:18:53,632 --> 00:18:56,176
Nanny, Uncle, I'll be right back.

315
00:18:56,260 --> 00:18:57,678
But…

316
00:18:57,761 --> 00:18:59,847
-I hope this helps. I'm sorry.
-Thank you.

317
00:19:01,390 --> 00:19:04,852
Thank you, Ms. Ivy.
To the Ardientes as well.

318
00:19:04,935 --> 00:19:07,104
We're sorry about what happened.

319
00:19:07,187 --> 00:19:09,731
Some of our friends
are just really violent.

320
00:19:10,315 --> 00:19:13,402
They should've listened.
They shouldn't have fought back.

321
00:19:13,485 --> 00:19:14,945
There wouldn't have been any trouble.

322
00:19:15,028 --> 00:19:16,655
Again, I'm sorry.

323
00:19:16,738 --> 00:19:18,782
-[Diego] Ms. Aguas.
-[women] Thank you.

324
00:19:18,866 --> 00:19:20,075
What are you doing here?

325
00:19:20,659 --> 00:19:22,786
Um… Mr. Torillo.

326
00:19:22,870 --> 00:19:26,540
Can you just leave?
Don't try to fool the farmers.

327
00:19:26,623 --> 00:19:28,750
You're only after the land, right?

328
00:19:31,628 --> 00:19:34,381
Mr. Torillo, I'm here
because I want to help--

329
00:19:34,464 --> 00:19:35,465
You want to help?

330
00:19:36,717 --> 00:19:38,218
Then leave Ardiente!

331
00:19:39,887 --> 00:19:41,430
But of course, you won't do that.

332
00:19:41,513 --> 00:19:43,140
Because money is more important to you

333
00:19:43,724 --> 00:19:45,851
than the welfare of these farmers!

334
00:19:46,351 --> 00:19:48,437
The harvest destroyed last night?

335
00:19:48,520 --> 00:19:50,105
That was from the blood
and sweat of these farmers!

336
00:19:50,189 --> 00:19:52,566
It's where they get the money
for their children's education!

337
00:19:52,649 --> 00:19:54,902
Treatment for their sick parents!

338
00:19:54,985 --> 00:19:56,486
And for their food!

339
00:19:56,570 --> 00:20:00,115
And these people you're helping…
look them in the eye!

340
00:20:00,199 --> 00:20:02,534
All of them will lose
their livelihood and homes!

341
00:20:04,036 --> 00:20:05,621
You're smart enough to see that.

342
00:20:06,747 --> 00:20:08,040
And you're beautiful too.

343
00:20:12,628 --> 00:20:15,255
It's a shame you don't have a good heart.

344
00:20:16,590 --> 00:20:19,927
[instrumental theme music playing]

345
00:20:27,559 --> 00:20:30,020
I understand where you're
coming from, Mr. Torillo.

346
00:20:32,940 --> 00:20:36,735
If you want me to leave… then I will.

347
00:20:38,153 --> 00:20:42,658
I only ask you not to doubt
that I really do want to help.

348
00:20:49,623 --> 00:20:52,209
Take your money when you leave too.

349
00:20:52,292 --> 00:20:54,544
So the project here won't push through.

350
00:20:56,672 --> 00:21:00,467
[instrumental theme music playing]

351
00:21:14,314 --> 00:21:15,857
[Emilia] Arnaldo!

352
00:21:15,941 --> 00:21:17,609
That brother of yours

353
00:21:17,693 --> 00:21:20,779
knows nothing better
than to taint our family's name!

354
00:21:21,989 --> 00:21:23,156
And where is your father?

355
00:21:24,741 --> 00:21:25,742
Oh, there he is.

356
00:21:25,826 --> 00:21:29,037
Raul, do you know
what your wonderful son did?

357
00:21:29,121 --> 00:21:30,330
I'm sure you don't.

358
00:21:30,414 --> 00:21:33,959
Because if you were home, you'd
know what's been going on here!

359
00:21:34,042 --> 00:21:37,087
-Mom.
-What? It's the truth!

360
00:21:37,170 --> 00:21:38,380
Where are you going now?

361
00:21:39,256 --> 00:21:40,257
Raul!

362
00:21:42,050 --> 00:21:43,010
[sighs]

363
00:21:43,969 --> 00:21:45,721
Arnaldo, there's nothing I can do

364
00:21:45,804 --> 00:21:48,432
about your father and brother anymore.

365
00:21:48,515 --> 00:21:50,142
We should clean this mess up instead.

366
00:21:50,851 --> 00:21:54,938
You know what? All I can think about…
is Ivy.

367
00:21:55,022 --> 00:21:58,400
Now, she has more reasons
not to push through with the project.

368
00:21:58,483 --> 00:22:00,485
Does your grandpa know about this yet?

369
00:22:00,569 --> 00:22:03,613
-I was about to tell him.
-No. Don't tell him yet, okay?

370
00:22:04,323 --> 00:22:06,575
Let's fix this ourselves. [sighs]

371
00:22:06,658 --> 00:22:10,912
-I'll go talk to Ivy, okay?
-I'll talk to her, Mom.

372
00:22:10,996 --> 00:22:11,997
What?

373
00:22:12,080 --> 00:22:13,498
-I'll do it.
-Are you serious?

374
00:22:13,582 --> 00:22:16,001
Did you forget you have lunch
with Natalie today?

375
00:22:16,084 --> 00:22:18,587
-What?
-Come on, Arnaldo.

376
00:22:18,670 --> 00:22:20,756
You can't push Natalie aside.

377
00:22:20,839 --> 00:22:23,925
We need her for our political mission.

378
00:22:24,009 --> 00:22:26,428
So focus. Okay?

379
00:22:31,058 --> 00:22:31,933
Good morning, Auntie.

380
00:22:32,017 --> 00:22:33,685
-Oh, Natalie, you're here.
-Hi.

381
00:22:33,769 --> 00:22:37,272
Great timing.
Arnaldo's ready for your lunch.

382
00:22:37,355 --> 00:22:39,608
-Great. Let's go?
-[Emilia] Go!

383
00:22:39,691 --> 00:22:40,734
Let's go.

384
00:22:42,319 --> 00:22:44,446
-Good morning, Mayor.
-Good morning, Chief.

385
00:22:44,529 --> 00:22:47,199
-Chief.
-Gov. Good news.

386
00:22:47,282 --> 00:22:50,994
We have a suspect for desecration
of the Congressman's statue.

387
00:22:51,078 --> 00:22:52,287
Really?

388
00:22:52,370 --> 00:22:54,498
You won't believe who this person is.

389
00:22:54,581 --> 00:22:56,083
Who is it?

390
00:22:56,166 --> 00:22:58,210
Uh, where's Congressman?

391
00:22:58,877 --> 00:23:03,090
It'll be better if I show the report
to all three of you together.

392
00:23:03,173 --> 00:23:05,092
-Okay.
-All right. Uh…

393
00:23:05,175 --> 00:23:06,885
Natalie, I'm sorry,
but I have to deal with this first.

394
00:23:07,594 --> 00:23:10,680
Uh, okay. Um, I understand.

395
00:23:10,764 --> 00:23:12,349
I'll make it up to you.

396
00:23:12,432 --> 00:23:13,683
Madrigal, please escort Natalie.

397
00:23:13,767 --> 00:23:15,268
-Bye.
-Let's go, Chief.

398
00:23:15,352 --> 00:23:16,353
-Chief. Let's go.
-All right.

399
00:23:23,193 --> 00:23:27,280
Nanny, I feel I need to do something.

400
00:23:27,364 --> 00:23:28,907
I have to make it up to them.

401
00:23:31,660 --> 00:23:33,411
I can talk to Emilia.

402
00:23:34,287 --> 00:23:40,335
Maybe I should ask her to build
the project on a different lot,

403
00:23:40,418 --> 00:23:42,712
so the farmers can keep their land.

404
00:23:42,796 --> 00:23:45,048
What if she refuses?

405
00:23:45,632 --> 00:23:47,467
If she does…

406
00:23:47,551 --> 00:23:49,636
then I'll pull out of my investment.

407
00:23:50,387 --> 00:23:53,098
Ivy, is that even possible?

408
00:23:53,181 --> 00:23:55,267
You might anger the Ardientes.

409
00:23:55,350 --> 00:23:59,938
Anger them? The Ardientes
can't get mad at me.

410
00:24:00,021 --> 00:24:02,482
I can tear them down.

411
00:24:02,566 --> 00:24:04,401
I can expose their lies.

412
00:24:05,527 --> 00:24:06,736
[Jepoy] Ivy, hold it.

413
00:24:08,280 --> 00:24:09,948
Before you do that,
you need to know something.

414
00:24:10,699 --> 00:24:11,616
What is it?

415
00:24:13,785 --> 00:24:16,037
Someone saw you destroying the statue.

416
00:24:16,121 --> 00:24:18,331
What?! Who saw me?

417
00:24:18,415 --> 00:24:20,876
His name is Arthur. He's nuts.

418
00:24:21,376 --> 00:24:24,087
Don't worry, no one will believe him.

419
00:24:26,173 --> 00:24:27,966
Arthur? Nuts?

420
00:24:29,885 --> 00:24:32,179
Arthur?

421
00:24:33,138 --> 00:24:34,723
His name sounds familiar.

422
00:24:35,390 --> 00:24:36,474
[Camia] Come on, hon.

423
00:24:36,558 --> 00:24:40,979
Your co-workers did say
Arthur has a mental condition.

424
00:24:42,981 --> 00:24:44,399
Arthur…

425
00:24:45,192 --> 00:24:47,569
My father used to have
a co-worker with that name.

426
00:24:47,652 --> 00:24:48,695
Exactly.

427
00:24:48,778 --> 00:24:49,905
It's him?

428
00:24:50,906 --> 00:24:52,240
I found these in his house.

429
00:25:00,624 --> 00:25:01,875
These are my father's files.

430
00:25:03,627 --> 00:25:05,045
Why does Arthur have them?

431
00:25:05,795 --> 00:25:06,963
I've been wondering that too.

432
00:25:08,840 --> 00:25:11,843
Aside from that, I saw
some dynamite in his house.

433
00:25:12,427 --> 00:25:14,804
Seems like he's plotting
something against the Ardientes.

434
00:25:18,225 --> 00:25:20,352
Arthur was Dad's co-worker.

435
00:25:22,354 --> 00:25:26,233
It's possible he knew something
about Dad's plans against the Ardientes.

436
00:25:26,316 --> 00:25:30,362
And when Dad died, he took all his files…

437
00:25:30,445 --> 00:25:32,906
to accomplish my father's plans.

438
00:25:35,033 --> 00:25:36,284
Jepoy, here's what you should do.

439
00:25:38,245 --> 00:25:40,914
Before the Ardientes
discover Arthur's plan,

440
00:25:40,997 --> 00:25:43,708
you need to take him away from here.

441
00:25:43,792 --> 00:25:46,962
[action music playing]

442
00:25:51,925 --> 00:25:53,426
[Julio] Where did you get these?

443
00:25:53,927 --> 00:25:56,054
My men followed him, Congressman.

444
00:25:56,972 --> 00:25:59,683
Those pictures were taken near his house.

445
00:26:00,267 --> 00:26:02,811
You mean this lunatic
is the one going against us?

446
00:26:04,229 --> 00:26:06,022
So, where is this man now?

447
00:26:06,106 --> 00:26:07,857
He's been detained, Congressman.

448
00:26:07,941 --> 00:26:09,192
Oh, I see.

449
00:26:10,151 --> 00:26:11,194
[Julio] So…

450
00:26:11,778 --> 00:26:15,699
-Can you bring him here?
-Of course, sir.

451
00:26:15,782 --> 00:26:17,742
And one more thing.

452
00:26:17,826 --> 00:26:21,871
Could you tell your men…

453
00:26:22,372 --> 00:26:25,583
to burn all the documents, and pictures…

454
00:26:26,543 --> 00:26:29,462
that they find in his house?

455
00:26:29,546 --> 00:26:31,131
-Yes, sir.
-Thank you.

456
00:26:31,214 --> 00:26:32,549
No problem, sir.

457
00:26:36,553 --> 00:26:37,887
[grunting]

458
00:26:40,223 --> 00:26:43,685
[tense music playing]

459
00:26:45,937 --> 00:26:50,692
I thought you already got rid of that man.

460
00:26:51,943 --> 00:26:58,616
Didn't he work as a clerk
in the public lawyer's office?

461
00:27:00,243 --> 00:27:02,620
He must know something about us, then.

462
00:27:02,704 --> 00:27:08,043
And about what you did to Atty. Cruz.

463
00:27:08,793 --> 00:27:11,254
Of course, Papa.
But as far as I'm concerned…

464
00:27:11,338 --> 00:27:15,050
Atty. Cruz died of heart attack
while driving.

465
00:27:15,133 --> 00:27:19,763
Besides, we shouldn't
waste our time on this man.

466
00:27:19,846 --> 00:27:24,392
He just wanders around town,
but he will do us no harm, Papa.

467
00:27:24,476 --> 00:27:26,102
You know what?

468
00:27:26,186 --> 00:27:28,605
We should just send him
to a mental institution.

469
00:27:28,688 --> 00:27:30,523
Hold on. I'll call the doctor.

470
00:27:31,232 --> 00:27:32,817
-[tense music playing]
-Ouch!

471
00:27:33,443 --> 00:27:35,653
You better be thankful that's all I did.

472
00:27:37,489 --> 00:27:40,742
It's your fault for not using your head.

473
00:27:41,451 --> 00:27:45,747
Do you really think a nutjob like him…

474
00:27:45,830 --> 00:27:48,583
is capable of doing all this alone, huh?

475
00:27:48,666 --> 00:27:49,834
Grandpa…

476
00:27:50,627 --> 00:27:52,045
you mean he's got an accomplice?

477
00:27:52,128 --> 00:27:53,171
Definitely.

478
00:27:53,254 --> 00:27:55,382
-Let me handle him, Papa.
-No.

479
00:27:55,465 --> 00:27:56,883
Stop it.

480
00:27:56,966 --> 00:28:00,887
I don't want you
to be involved in any of this anymore.

481
00:28:02,305 --> 00:28:04,307
Emilia, you disappoint me.

482
00:28:05,392 --> 00:28:06,643
You…

483
00:28:07,227 --> 00:28:09,062
and your worthless husband…

484
00:28:09,646 --> 00:28:11,439
really deserve each other.

485
00:28:12,399 --> 00:28:15,443
Arnaldo's the only one I can rely on.

486
00:28:21,157 --> 00:28:23,576
Get out of my face. Go! Now!

487
00:28:40,760 --> 00:28:42,178
No!

488
00:28:42,262 --> 00:28:45,807
[tense music playing]

489
00:28:49,394 --> 00:28:51,062
Arthur? Arthur?

490
00:28:52,272 --> 00:28:53,314
Arthur?

491
00:28:55,525 --> 00:28:59,237
[eerie music playing]

492
00:29:06,578 --> 00:29:08,204
[action music playing]

493
00:29:08,288 --> 00:29:10,665
[cop 1] The Chief said to burn all papers.

494
00:29:10,749 --> 00:29:11,791
[cop 2] Okay, sir.

495
00:29:19,966 --> 00:29:21,176
Let's do this.

496
00:29:21,259 --> 00:29:22,427
All right.

497
00:29:27,474 --> 00:29:32,228
Well, I'm sure you've calmed down
after taking a bath.

498
00:29:34,147 --> 00:29:37,192
Everyone's talking about
what you said to Ms. Ivy.

499
00:29:37,275 --> 00:29:41,362
Nanny, I only told her
the things she had to hear.

500
00:29:41,946 --> 00:29:45,700
I understand, Diego.
But what you did was--

501
00:29:45,784 --> 00:29:47,160
But Nanny…

502
00:29:47,243 --> 00:29:49,329
I couldn't control myself.

503
00:29:49,913 --> 00:29:52,791
I think it's better
if she just leaves this place.

504
00:29:54,417 --> 00:29:55,794
Do you think she'll listen to you?

505
00:29:57,045 --> 00:29:59,047
What will you do if she doesn't?

506
00:30:04,969 --> 00:30:07,263
How about this? Why don't you…

507
00:30:07,347 --> 00:30:11,476
you know… talk to Ms. Ivy?

508
00:30:11,559 --> 00:30:13,102
Do it now.

509
00:30:13,186 --> 00:30:14,145
[sniffing]

510
00:30:14,229 --> 00:30:17,440
While you are fresh from the shower
and smelling so good!

511
00:30:17,524 --> 00:30:20,652
I'm sure she'll give in!

512
00:30:20,735 --> 00:30:23,029
Nanny, was that another one of your jokes?

513
00:30:23,112 --> 00:30:25,740
[laughs] No, I meant that!

514
00:30:26,533 --> 00:30:28,827
[Loring laughs] See, you're laughing now!

515
00:30:28,910 --> 00:30:29,994
Just try it.

516
00:30:31,037 --> 00:30:34,040
There's nothing a good talk can't fix.

517
00:30:34,123 --> 00:30:36,793
[pensive music playing]

518
00:30:40,421 --> 00:30:44,050
I think the Ardientes
got their hands on Arthur first.

519
00:30:44,133 --> 00:30:46,302
What do they plan to do with him?

520
00:30:46,386 --> 00:30:48,346
He's mentally incapacitated!

521
00:30:49,097 --> 00:30:50,139
Nanny…

522
00:30:50,223 --> 00:30:52,684
The Ardientes are ruthless.

523
00:30:52,767 --> 00:30:56,229
They won't hesitate to take down
anyone who gets in their way.

524
00:30:58,481 --> 00:30:59,816
Jepoy.

525
00:30:59,899 --> 00:31:01,359
We have to save Arthur.

526
00:31:02,277 --> 00:31:03,486
Leave it to me.

527
00:31:03,570 --> 00:31:04,779
[Ivy] No.

528
00:31:04,863 --> 00:31:07,240
-I'm coming with you.
-What?

529
00:31:07,323 --> 00:31:09,409
[action music playing]

530
00:31:10,827 --> 00:31:12,036
Grandpa, we have him.

531
00:31:14,497 --> 00:31:16,791
You know what to do.

532
00:31:17,834 --> 00:31:19,377
Don't delay it.

533
00:31:20,587 --> 00:31:22,338
Put an end to this.

534
00:31:22,422 --> 00:31:23,464
Yes, Grandpa.

535
00:31:27,927 --> 00:31:32,015
[tense music playing]

536
00:31:47,530 --> 00:31:49,240
[doorbell ringing]

537
00:31:53,703 --> 00:31:55,872
-Are we expecting anyone?
-No one.

538
00:31:55,955 --> 00:31:57,415
Who could it be?

539
00:32:04,881 --> 00:32:05,757
Diego?

540
00:32:08,885 --> 00:32:10,470
[crickets chirping]

541
00:32:10,553 --> 00:32:13,306
[engine running]

542
00:32:14,557 --> 00:32:16,893
[somber music playing]

543
00:32:22,440 --> 00:32:24,567
-Mom?
-Diego.

544
00:32:25,526 --> 00:32:26,569
What are you doing here?

545
00:32:30,156 --> 00:32:33,534
Now Emilia too? What are they doing here?

546
00:32:34,369 --> 00:32:35,286
I have to go, Ivy.

547
00:32:36,412 --> 00:32:37,830
Entertain them first.

548
00:32:38,456 --> 00:32:39,624
I swear, I'll save Arthur.

549
00:32:39,707 --> 00:32:40,708
Be careful.

550
00:32:42,043 --> 00:32:44,921
[tense music playing]

551
00:32:48,758 --> 00:32:50,009
What are you doing here?

552
00:32:51,302 --> 00:32:53,012
I wanted to talk to Ms. Aguas.

553
00:32:53,930 --> 00:32:56,307
About the export processing zone.

554
00:32:57,266 --> 00:33:01,604
Diego, don't stick your nose
where it doesn't belong.

555
00:33:01,688 --> 00:33:03,731
-But Mom…
-Leave.

556
00:33:04,941 --> 00:33:06,109
Leave now, Diego.

557
00:33:06,192 --> 00:33:07,443
Mom.

558
00:33:07,527 --> 00:33:08,736
I said leave.

559
00:33:11,114 --> 00:33:12,490
[door opening]

560
00:33:12,573 --> 00:33:13,574
Governor?

561
00:33:13,658 --> 00:33:14,867
[Emilia] Ivy.

562
00:33:16,869 --> 00:33:17,787
-Go on, son.
-Mister…

563
00:33:17,870 --> 00:33:20,790
[Emilia] You may go now.
I'll call you once I'm done.

564
00:33:20,873 --> 00:33:21,916
Mr. Torillo?

565
00:33:22,000 --> 00:33:22,834
-[Emilia] No, no, no.
-Why--

566
00:33:22,917 --> 00:33:23,918
[Emilia] It's nothing. Um…

567
00:33:24,002 --> 00:33:25,545
He just asked me something.

568
00:33:25,628 --> 00:33:27,005
Go now. You take care, okay?

569
00:33:32,552 --> 00:33:33,553
Let's go?

570
00:33:35,138 --> 00:33:36,472
Oh. Okay.

571
00:33:37,306 --> 00:33:39,183
-Here. I brought wine.
-Come in.

572
00:33:39,267 --> 00:33:43,396
[tense music playing]

573
00:33:51,320 --> 00:33:52,488
[ominous music playing]

574
00:33:52,572 --> 00:33:53,740
-[Arnaldo grunts]
-[Arthur screaming]

575
00:33:53,823 --> 00:33:54,824
[whipping]

576
00:33:54,907 --> 00:33:58,661
-[whipping]
-[screaming and grunting]

577
00:33:58,745 --> 00:33:59,954
You murderer!

578
00:34:00,788 --> 00:34:02,457
You demon!

579
00:34:03,499 --> 00:34:06,461
Your soul will burn in hell!

580
00:34:07,211 --> 00:34:09,255
-[Arthur groans]
-You know what…

581
00:34:09,338 --> 00:34:11,924
I'm only wasting my time on you because…

582
00:34:12,008 --> 00:34:16,512
I want to personally hear you
spill the information I need.

583
00:34:16,596 --> 00:34:18,264
But don't worry.

584
00:34:18,347 --> 00:34:21,350
I'll send you
to hell once I'm done with you.

585
00:34:22,018 --> 00:34:23,561
Why?

586
00:34:23,644 --> 00:34:24,937
What are you going to do to me?!

587
00:34:25,021 --> 00:34:28,816
-What will you do to me?
-It depends.

588
00:34:29,484 --> 00:34:31,611
It all depends on your answer.

589
00:34:31,694 --> 00:34:33,279
[Arthur whimpering]

590
00:34:33,863 --> 00:34:38,284
Because I don't believe that
you did this all on your own.

591
00:34:41,287 --> 00:34:43,414
And I don't believe you're crazy.

592
00:34:45,208 --> 00:34:47,126
I know you're just pretending.

593
00:34:47,960 --> 00:34:49,587
So, you should tell me…

594
00:34:51,255 --> 00:34:54,217
whom your boss is. Who ordered you?

595
00:34:54,300 --> 00:34:57,178
[ominous music playing]

596
00:34:57,804 --> 00:35:01,099
[laughing]

597
00:35:02,183 --> 00:35:04,018
[cries] I don't know anything.

598
00:35:05,061 --> 00:35:08,106
I don't know anything.
I don't know anything!

599
00:35:08,189 --> 00:35:09,524
Who ordered you?

600
00:35:09,607 --> 00:35:11,776
[action music playing]

601
00:35:11,859 --> 00:35:14,237
[whimpering]

602
00:35:16,948 --> 00:35:17,824
I'll talk!

603
00:35:18,783 --> 00:35:21,911
I'll talk! I'll talk! I'll talk!

604
00:35:21,994 --> 00:35:24,539
I'll talk!

605
00:35:24,622 --> 00:35:26,999
So, what brings you here?

606
00:35:27,667 --> 00:35:30,336
I came here to celebrate with my friend.

607
00:35:30,920 --> 00:35:33,005
Celebrate? What?

608
00:35:33,089 --> 00:35:35,133
[chuckles] Didn't you hear?

609
00:35:36,134 --> 00:35:37,176
About what?

610
00:35:38,344 --> 00:35:41,556
We arrested the culprit who
destroyed my father's statue.

611
00:35:41,639 --> 00:35:43,933
You did? Please sit down.

612
00:35:44,016 --> 00:35:45,268
Yes!

613
00:35:45,351 --> 00:35:48,646
And it turns out the man
was full-on crazy.

614
00:35:50,857 --> 00:35:53,484
Crazy? Was this all a prank?

615
00:35:53,568 --> 00:35:56,279
So, where is he?
In a psychiatric hospital?

616
00:35:57,029 --> 00:35:58,322
I don't know.

617
00:35:58,406 --> 00:35:59,907
But one thing's for sure.

618
00:36:00,533 --> 00:36:02,451
He'll pay for what he did.

619
00:36:02,535 --> 00:36:04,829
[sighs deeply]

620
00:36:04,912 --> 00:36:09,083
I have a feeling that tonight
is going to be my lucky night!

621
00:36:09,667 --> 00:36:10,877
You know why?

622
00:36:10,960 --> 00:36:14,589
Lots of good things
are happening to our family.

623
00:36:14,672 --> 00:36:17,633
First, the suspect who destroyed
the statue was caught.

624
00:36:17,717 --> 00:36:22,096
And tonight, you're going
to sign this contract, Ivy.

625
00:36:22,180 --> 00:36:25,183
[tense music playing]

626
00:36:27,351 --> 00:36:28,311
[chuckles]

627
00:36:30,062 --> 00:36:32,273
Governor, don't be in a rush.

628
00:36:32,356 --> 00:36:35,860
Maybe we should take
a sip of your wine first.

629
00:36:36,652 --> 00:36:38,529
And if I like it,

630
00:36:38,613 --> 00:36:41,240
then I might be convinced
to sign that contract.

631
00:36:41,824 --> 00:36:43,910
I don't need wine for that.

632
00:36:45,953 --> 00:36:47,163
Are you sure?

633
00:36:49,207 --> 00:36:52,210
Didn't Arnaldo tell you that

634
00:36:52,293 --> 00:36:54,879
I'm not easy to please?

635
00:36:57,173 --> 00:36:58,507
Try me.

636
00:37:12,146 --> 00:37:13,481
Good.

637
00:37:13,564 --> 00:37:15,816
[labored breathing]

638
00:37:15,900 --> 00:37:17,443
Now spill.

639
00:37:20,404 --> 00:37:26,661
The savior has arrived
to bring you to your knees!

640
00:37:27,578 --> 00:37:30,164
-[laughing]
-[screams, whips]

641
00:37:30,248 --> 00:37:31,582
-[laughing]
-[Arnaldo screaming]

642
00:37:31,666 --> 00:37:33,876
No one messes with my grandfather!

643
00:37:33,960 --> 00:37:34,961
[laughing]

644
00:37:36,170 --> 00:37:37,713
No one messes with my grandfather!

645
00:37:37,797 --> 00:37:39,548
-[Arnaldo screams, whips]
-[Arthur grunts, laughs]

646
00:37:39,632 --> 00:37:42,093
[screams, whips, laughing]

647
00:37:42,176 --> 00:37:45,137
I grew up with my grandfather
being respected!

648
00:37:45,221 --> 00:37:49,350
People fear him, and you have
the guts to mock him?

649
00:37:49,433 --> 00:37:51,143
[Arnaldo screams, whips]

650
00:37:51,227 --> 00:37:52,979
[Arthur groans]

651
00:37:53,062 --> 00:37:54,689
As long as I'm alive…

652
00:37:56,065 --> 00:37:57,775
no one can hurt my grandfather.

653
00:37:59,235 --> 00:38:00,236
-No one!
-[grunts]

654
00:38:01,320 --> 00:38:04,865
[tense music playing]

655
00:38:04,949 --> 00:38:08,619
[labored breathing]

656
00:38:10,413 --> 00:38:13,082
[Emilia] So, how do you like the wine?

657
00:38:13,874 --> 00:38:15,626
It's okay, it's sweet.

658
00:38:16,377 --> 00:38:17,336
But…

659
00:38:19,130 --> 00:38:20,756
it's too light.

660
00:38:20,840 --> 00:38:22,133
In terms of a person…

661
00:38:22,883 --> 00:38:24,468
it's as ineffective…

662
00:38:25,720 --> 00:38:26,929
as a bootlicker.

663
00:38:28,097 --> 00:38:29,098
[sighs]

664
00:38:30,099 --> 00:38:33,811
On the contrary,
this is how I like my wine to be.

665
00:38:34,437 --> 00:38:35,771
Sweet.

666
00:38:35,855 --> 00:38:37,732
But has quite the kick?

667
00:38:38,524 --> 00:38:39,817
It's more like me.

668
00:38:40,443 --> 00:38:41,902
Should I be nervous?

669
00:38:42,987 --> 00:38:46,741
Ivy, what's important
is we understand each other.

670
00:38:47,742 --> 00:38:52,580
So, why don't you sign
our deal, the contract right there,

671
00:38:52,663 --> 00:38:55,750
so we both live happily ever after?

672
00:38:57,918 --> 00:38:59,003
[laughs]

673
00:38:59,962 --> 00:39:02,214
[somber music playing]

674
00:39:02,798 --> 00:39:06,469
I don't live in fairy tales…

675
00:39:07,094 --> 00:39:10,848
nor do I believe in happily-ever-afters.

676
00:39:11,974 --> 00:39:13,476
I live in what's real…

677
00:39:15,019 --> 00:39:17,897
and where I'm sure I'm safe.

678
00:39:18,856 --> 00:39:22,401
[laughing]

679
00:39:23,527 --> 00:39:27,490
Ivy, how can I protect you
if you're going against me?

680
00:39:27,573 --> 00:39:30,201
What? Against you?

681
00:39:31,535 --> 00:39:33,496
Governor, we're friends!

682
00:39:33,579 --> 00:39:35,706
Didn't I save your life?

683
00:39:36,374 --> 00:39:38,000
I know, that's why I trust you.

684
00:39:38,584 --> 00:39:40,252
I know you won't push me

685
00:39:40,336 --> 00:39:43,464
to do something I'll regret in the end.

686
00:39:45,007 --> 00:39:49,553
[tense music playing]

687
00:39:54,183 --> 00:39:55,267
-[sighs]
-Arnaldo.

688
00:39:58,229 --> 00:39:59,188
What is it, Diego?

689
00:39:59,855 --> 00:40:01,899
I want to talk to you and Grandpa.

690
00:40:02,483 --> 00:40:03,734
I'm busy, Diego. Maybe tomorrow.

691
00:40:03,818 --> 00:40:06,445
If you won't talk to me,
I'll go straight to Grandpa.

692
00:40:06,529 --> 00:40:09,698
You have the same opinions
and decisions anyway.

693
00:40:11,867 --> 00:40:14,370
If this is about the export
processing zone again,

694
00:40:14,453 --> 00:40:16,205
you're just wasting your breath.

695
00:40:16,288 --> 00:40:19,834
It's better than not using it.

696
00:40:24,046 --> 00:40:26,632
-See you.
-Arnaldo

697
00:40:26,715 --> 00:40:29,677
[tense music playing]

698
00:40:31,137 --> 00:40:32,596
Whatever it is you're up to…

699
00:40:33,806 --> 00:40:35,933
I hope you think it over.

700
00:40:39,562 --> 00:40:41,147
Who are you to give me advice?

701
00:40:42,523 --> 00:40:45,526
I'm the mayor. And you?

702
00:40:46,193 --> 00:40:48,696
I'm the Ardiente who cares
about the people.

703
00:40:56,579 --> 00:40:58,956
[Emilia] <i>So, Ivy, what do you have to say?</i>

704
00:40:59,039 --> 00:41:02,293
Is it a yes or yes?

705
00:41:05,296 --> 00:41:07,423
I want to say yes, but…

706
00:41:08,215 --> 00:41:10,926
like what I said,
my lawyers have to look it over.

707
00:41:12,178 --> 00:41:13,179
[sighs]

708
00:41:14,346 --> 00:41:17,600
You know, Ivy… from the looks of it…

709
00:41:18,184 --> 00:41:20,060
you're giving me a hard time.

710
00:41:20,144 --> 00:41:23,272
You are making me beg,
and I'm not liking it.

711
00:41:23,355 --> 00:41:25,858
To be honest, if the congressman

712
00:41:25,941 --> 00:41:29,945
was the one who asked me,
I might say yes to him.

713
00:41:30,029 --> 00:41:31,655
But I am the governor!

714
00:41:31,739 --> 00:41:34,575
And the governor
is as powerful as the congressman!

715
00:41:34,658 --> 00:41:37,495
You're only a governor in name.

716
00:41:38,370 --> 00:41:42,041
I can see how you let your father

717
00:41:42,124 --> 00:41:44,335
and even your son boss you around.

718
00:41:44,418 --> 00:41:49,131
It's like you just go to the
office to sign, give orders--

719
00:41:49,215 --> 00:41:51,800
Shut up! You don't know
what you're talking about!

720
00:41:51,884 --> 00:41:53,552
Of course I know what I'm saying!

721
00:41:53,636 --> 00:41:56,972
If you say you're good
at persuading people, well,

722
00:41:57,056 --> 00:41:59,266
I'm good at reading them.

723
00:41:59,350 --> 00:42:01,268
And I can read you like a book,
Governor Emilia.

724
00:42:01,352 --> 00:42:03,312
From head to toe.

725
00:42:06,106 --> 00:42:07,107
[sighs]

726
00:42:07,191 --> 00:42:08,692
[somber piano music playing]

727
00:42:08,776 --> 00:42:11,737
Impressive!

728
00:42:11,820 --> 00:42:13,364
[laughing]

729
00:42:15,074 --> 00:42:17,451
You just impressed me, Miss Aguas.

730
00:42:18,410 --> 00:42:19,703
For the first time…

731
00:42:20,913 --> 00:42:25,918
I met another woman as powerful as me.

732
00:42:26,585 --> 00:42:30,422
Someone who is straightforward,
doesn't suck up to me,

733
00:42:30,506 --> 00:42:34,760
and only tells the truth,
which is what I really like.

734
00:42:41,475 --> 00:42:44,520
[tense music playing]

735
00:42:57,700 --> 00:42:59,118
Diego…

736
00:43:00,077 --> 00:43:02,538
Let's not tire each other out.

737
00:43:04,290 --> 00:43:06,709
The project will push through.

738
00:43:07,459 --> 00:43:09,670
And that is final.

739
00:43:12,381 --> 00:43:13,382
Grandpa.

740
00:43:14,133 --> 00:43:16,343
Is there any way to change your mind?

741
00:43:17,052 --> 00:43:18,846
You've disappointed me enough, Diego.

742
00:43:20,598 --> 00:43:22,975
I have given up all hope…

743
00:43:24,184 --> 00:43:29,189
that you have anything good
to offer our family.

744
00:43:33,444 --> 00:43:34,862
Thank you for your time.

745
00:43:35,487 --> 00:43:36,488
But the truth is…

746
00:43:37,448 --> 00:43:39,450
I knew you were going to say these things.

747
00:43:41,118 --> 00:43:45,122
I only wanted to see
if I'd be able to change your mind.

748
00:43:46,040 --> 00:43:46,874
Grandpa…

749
00:43:48,125 --> 00:43:52,129
you have so many loyalists
who support and believe in you.

750
00:43:52,713 --> 00:43:55,966
I thought that maybe they see
something in you that I don't.

751
00:43:56,050 --> 00:43:58,218
What could they see in you?

752
00:43:58,302 --> 00:44:00,888
Because no matter
how I look at it, I see nothing.

753
00:44:00,971 --> 00:44:02,389
I don't see anything.

754
00:44:02,473 --> 00:44:03,641
So…

755
00:44:04,266 --> 00:44:05,392
Grandpa, we're even.

756
00:44:05,476 --> 00:44:09,313
Because if I disappointed
you, you disappointed me too.

757
00:44:11,273 --> 00:44:12,107
But…

758
00:44:13,400 --> 00:44:19,448
But, Grandpa, I hope
that one day, you can change.

759
00:44:19,531 --> 00:44:21,158
[tense music playing]

760
00:44:27,956 --> 00:44:31,794
You know… you just earned my respect.

761
00:44:31,877 --> 00:44:33,045
[scoffs]

762
00:44:34,129 --> 00:44:36,507
Governor, don't get me wrong.

763
00:44:36,590 --> 00:44:38,884
I didn't say that to belittle you.

764
00:44:38,967 --> 00:44:43,305
The truth is I want you
to be brave as a woman.

765
00:44:44,890 --> 00:44:49,061
Someone who can fight back and win.

766
00:44:51,939 --> 00:44:56,193
-But I can win if I want to.
-Exactly!

767
00:44:56,276 --> 00:44:59,696
Exactly, Governor,
but it's difficult, isn't it?

768
00:45:01,031 --> 00:45:02,491
I know it is.

769
00:45:03,492 --> 00:45:04,701
I know the hardships

770
00:45:04,785 --> 00:45:08,664
a woman faces in this world
governed by men.

771
00:45:09,248 --> 00:45:11,208
I went through those things
doing business.

772
00:45:11,792 --> 00:45:12,793
And I succeeded.

773
00:45:14,420 --> 00:45:17,965
So, Governor, I want you to succeed too.

774
00:45:19,174 --> 00:45:22,136
Because you live in a world
surrounded by powerful men.

775
00:45:24,054 --> 00:45:27,516
It's tough because they're your family.

776
00:45:27,599 --> 00:45:28,892
But I know.

777
00:45:30,060 --> 00:45:34,022
I know you can keep up with them.

778
00:45:36,775 --> 00:45:39,778
I guess that's the curse on us women, huh?

779
00:45:40,362 --> 00:45:41,447
Especially on me.

780
00:45:43,282 --> 00:45:44,450
It's my family.

781
00:45:45,492 --> 00:45:51,498
Papa, my husband, my son…
They are all domineering.

782
00:45:54,668 --> 00:45:59,214
I only wanted for my father
to cheer for my success

783
00:45:59,298 --> 00:46:01,216
and not see the failure in me.

784
00:46:04,178 --> 00:46:06,346
I only want him to tell me…

785
00:46:08,432 --> 00:46:09,308
"I'm proud of you."

786
00:46:10,225 --> 00:46:11,810
But Papa…

787
00:46:12,436 --> 00:46:16,231
My father's heart is as hard as steel.

788
00:46:20,486 --> 00:46:23,197
But even steel can melt.

789
00:46:23,280 --> 00:46:26,909
[tense music playing]

790
00:46:26,992 --> 00:46:30,204
And you need to stand your ground.

791
00:46:30,287 --> 00:46:36,460
Maybe it's time you show them
that you can stand beside them.

792
00:46:37,127 --> 00:46:39,171
Not as a woman,

793
00:46:41,048 --> 00:46:44,092
but as their equal.

794
00:46:45,135 --> 00:46:49,097
As Governor Emilia, and as an Ardiente.

795
00:46:50,807 --> 00:46:52,893
You're more than capable.

796
00:47:08,951 --> 00:47:12,371
[Julio] You're a governor!
You have no self-respect!

797
00:47:12,454 --> 00:47:16,291
[Emilia] <i>You are right! I am the governor,</i>
<i>and I can do anything I want!</i>

798
00:47:16,375 --> 00:47:19,086
[Ivy] <i>Because tomorrow,</i>
<i>the Ardientes will wake up</i>

799
00:47:19,169 --> 00:47:22,339
<i>-to a living nightmare.</i>
-<i>The congressman's share!</i>

800
00:47:22,422 --> 00:47:24,216
<i>-Is this all of it?</i>
<i>-Give it to him.</i>

801
00:47:24,299 --> 00:47:26,426
<i>Is it true you're a gambling operator</i>
<i>and protector?</i>

802
00:47:26,510 --> 00:47:29,221
[Ivy] <i>If the issue spreads,</i>
<i>the media will swarm you,</i>

803
00:47:29,304 --> 00:47:31,807
<i>especially because you passed</i>
<i>the Anti-Gambling Bill.</i>

804
00:47:31,890 --> 00:47:35,018
<i>If I were you, I'd distance myself</i>
<i>from the congressman.</i>

805
00:47:35,102 --> 00:47:39,314
<i>You moron! This is all your fault!</i>

806
00:47:39,398 --> 00:47:41,149
-[Raul] <i>I'll kill you!</i>
<i>-Raul, stop!</i>

807
00:47:41,233 --> 00:47:44,403
[theme music playing]
